{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Jr.&limit=10&title=A Magic Web","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"A  "},"title":"magic web ","subTitle":"the forest of Barro Colorado Island "},"name":[{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Ziegler, Christian","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Leigh, Egbert Giles,",{"@type":"termsOfAddress","#text":"Jr.,"},{"@type":"date","#text":"1940-"}]}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Oxford "}},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York "}}],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Oxford University Press"},"dateIssued":"2002"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"xii, 292 pages : color illustrations ; 31 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"\"In A Magic Web, photographer Christian Ziegler and ecologist Egbert Giles Leigh, Jr., invite readers to enter the marvelous world of Barro Colorado Island. This book is a combination of photography and text written by an active scientist who has spent half a lifetime trying to understand the tropical forest. Photographs of the forest reveal the wonderful diversity of its inhabitants, and show many of the activities that give it its character and lend structure to its community. Drawing on decades of work on Barro Colorado Island, Egbert Leigh explains how the forest works.\"--Jacket."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"1. What Is Special about Tropical Forests? -- 2. The Life of Plants -- 3. Eating and Being Eaten -- 4. Animals -- 5. Why Tropical Forests Matter."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"photographs by Christian Ziegler ; text by Egbert Giles Leigh, Jr."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"ncpn---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Forest ecology","geographic":["Panama","Barro Colorado Island"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Ecology"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Trees"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Ecology"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Trees"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Écologie forestière","geographic":["Panamá","Barro Colorado, Île de"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Écologie"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Arbres"},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"ecology"},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"trees (woody plants)"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Trees"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Ecology"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Forest ecology"},{"@authority":"gnd","topic":"Tropischer Wald"},{"@authority":"gnd","topic":"Waldökosystem"},{"@authority":"rero","topic":"forêt","geographic":"Barro Colorado (Panama)"},{"@authority":"rero","topic":"forêt","geographic":"Barro Colorado (Panama)","genre":"photographies"},{"@authority":"mesh","geographic":"Barro Colorado Island"},{"@authority":"mesh","geographic":"Panama"},{"@authority":"fast","geographic":["Panama","Barro Colorado Island"]},{"@authority":"gnd","geographic":"Barro Colorado Island"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"QH108.P3 Z54 2002"},{"@edition":"21","@authority":"ddc","#text":"577.3/097287/32"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0195143280"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780195143287"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"2001055455"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"48383562"}],"rel